Z||000004||bcwawright||05-16-2001||12:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>Call Rodney Dickman and get his opinion.  He is quite familiar with them but I don't know he rebuilds them anymore.  He might have suggestions on where to bring it though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Called Rodney and he doesn't do it anymore..and he couldn't recommend anyone.<BR>He also said that some bearings were no longer available.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||05-16-2001||08:32 AM||||Maybe cheaper just to buy an used one. Check them out.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PJ||05-16-2001||10:19 AM||||Bruce,<P>What's wrong with it? I've rebuilt a few of them.<P>PJ<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||bcwawright||05-16-2001||10:26 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PJ:<BR><B>Bruce,<P>What's wrong with it? I've rebuilt a few of them.<P>PJ</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hi PJ<BR>The tranny appears to need bearing s on both sides and seals...you can move axle up and down and the axle on the other side moves...also leaking fluid...no cracks..looks like the thing just needs resealing<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||PJ||05-16-2001||10:33 AM||||The diff carrier bearings and axle seals are easy to replace if that's all it needs. I'll look at it for you if you can get it down here to Daytona. E-Mail me.<P>PJ<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||05-16-2001||11:31 AM||||Few of the dealers have someone trained on the Getrag. I had one rebuilt here in California and it was $1200. The brass alone was $600. <P>They prefer you buy a Goodwrench rebuild and frankly, that's what I would do. Beyond that, a used trans from a Fiero or Beretta (using Rodney's kit) is your only other choice. Again keep checking trans rebuilders.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000010||bcwawright||05-16-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Few of the dealers have someone trained on the Getrag. I had one rebuilt here in California and it was $1200. The brass alone was $600. <P>They prefer you buy a Goodwrench rebuild and frankly, that's what I would do. Beyond that, a used trans from a Fiero or Beretta (using Rodney's kit) is your only other choice. Again keep checking trans rebuilders.<P>TK</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the info. Does GM sell a rebuilt one that is for a Fiero? How much does a GM rebuilt one cost?<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica<P>||||reg||1
